cff-version: 1.2.0
title: eigen-portfolios
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hekimoglu
    given-names: Fatih
    email: fatih.hekim1@hotmail.com
abstract: >-
  A research-grade Python toolkit for principal component analysis of
  financial return correlation matrices, with Marchenko-Pastur random
  matrix theory used to separate signal eigenmodes from noise. Implements
  the spectrum estimator, the Marchenko-Pastur bulk PDF and edges, a
  maximum-likelihood noise-variance fit, sector-driven factor labelling,
  and validated against scikit-learn PCA, the closed-form Marchenko-Pastur
  edges, and the qualitative spectrum reported by Plerou et al. (1999).
keywords:
  - pca
  - random-matrix-theory
  - marchenko-pastur
  - quantitative-finance
  - eigen-portfolios
